IMPORTANT NOTICE
================================================================================
This document is a rights reservation and limited-license instrument for original
works in the Mermicorn Grove constellation. It is not a grant of open-source
rights. It is not legal advice. Cherry should have qualified counsel in Hawaiʻi
(or other relevant jurisdiction) review and customize this instrument before
relying on it for high-stakes commercial or enforcement use. Registration of
copyright with the U.S. Copyright Office strengthens remedies; consider it for
material works.

================================================================================
1. OWNER AND WORKS COVERED
================================================================================
1.1 Owner. The copyright owner of the original works described herein is Cherry
    (operating publicly as Cyber Lazer Mermicorn) ("Owner").

1.2 Covered Works. This instrument covers all original works of authorship
    created by or for Owner in connection with the Mermicorn Grove, including
    without limitation:
    (a) source code, object code, scripts, schemas, templates, and tooling;
    (b) documentation, contracts, READMEs, architecture, and process materials;
    (c) designs, concepts, mockups, tech packs, product packaging, and campaign
        assets (including ravewear and other creative collections);
    (d) commercial workflows, listing systems, pricing frameworks, and sales
        packages;
    (e) data models, prompts, agent configurations, and AI-assisted outputs
        directed by Owner;
    (f) branding, names, logos, and trade dress originated by Owner;
    (g) any other fixed original expression in the constellation repositories
        and related private materials.

1.3 Third-Party Materials. Third-party software, trademarks, game properties,
    marketplace platforms, and libraries remain the property of their respective
    owners. Fan or reference material is unaffiliated unless expressly stated.
    This instrument does not claim ownership of third-party rights.

================================================================================
2. LEGAL BASIS — RESERVATION OF RIGHTS
================================================================================
2.1 U.S. Copyright. Under Title 17 of the United States Code, including
    17 U.S.C. § 106, Owner holds the exclusive rights to reproduce, prepare
    derivative works, distribute copies, publicly perform, and publicly display
    the Covered Works (subject to statutory limitations such as fair use under
    § 107 and, where applicable, § 117 regarding computer programs).

2.2 Automatic Protection. Copyright protection attaches upon fixation of an
    original work in a tangible medium. Notice and the phrase "All rights
    reserved" are not required for protection under current U.S. law, but are
    used here for clarity and to defeat claims of implied license.

2.3 Reservation. ALL RIGHTS NOT EXPRESSLY GRANTED IN A SEPARATE WRITTEN
    INSTRUMENT SIGNED BY OWNER ARE RESERVED TO OWNER. Public availability of
    repositories or documents does not constitute a license to copy, modify,
    distribute, commercialize, or create derivative works beyond ordinary
    viewing and linking permitted by platform terms and applicable law.

2.4 No Implied License. Access to public GitHub content, reading documentation,
    or cloning for personal inspection does not grant any license beyond what
    GitHub’s terms and applicable law already allow. No license is granted by
    estoppel, course of dealing, or silence.

================================================================================
3. DEFAULT POSITION — NO GENERAL LICENSE
================================================================================
3.1 Default. Except as set forth in Section 4 (Limited Public Viewing) or in a
    separate written agreement signed by Owner, no person or entity is granted
    any license under this instrument to:
    (a) copy, reproduce, or mirror the Covered Works (except ephemeral copies
        incidental to ordinary viewing);
    (b) modify, adapt, translate, or create derivative works;
    (c) distribute, publish, sublicense, sell, lease, or otherwise transfer;
    (d) reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, or attempt to derive source
        code or underlying methods except to the limited extent such activity
        cannot be prohibited by applicable law;
    (e) remove, alter, or obscure copyright, trademark, or proprietary notices;
    (f) use the Covered Works for commercial purposes, training of competing
        commercial systems, or public redistribution;
    (g) use Owner’s names, marks, or trade dress in a manner that suggests
        endorsement or affiliation without prior written consent.

3.2 Software Specific. Where Covered Works include software, Owner does not
    transfer ownership of any copy. Licensee (if any under a separate agreement)
    receives only the limited rights expressly stated in that agreement. Owner
    retains title to all copies.

================================================================================
4. LIMITED PUBLIC VIEWING
================================================================================
4.1 Viewing. Members of the public may view public repository content on GitHub
    (or successor platforms) for informational and portfolio-evaluation purposes,
    subject to the platform’s terms of service and applicable law.

4.2 No Further Rights. Viewing does not authorize downloading for redistribution,
    incorporation into other products, commercial exploitation, or training of
    models for commercial competing products without a separate written license.

4.3 Fair Use. Nothing in this instrument limits rights that cannot be waived
    under applicable law, including fair use under 17 U.S.C. § 107.

================================================================================
5. COLLABORATION AND LICENSING PROCESS
================================================================================
5.1 Open to Discussion. Owner welcomes collaboration, contribution, partnership,
    and selective licensing discussions.

5.2 Required Form. Any grant of rights beyond Section 4 must be in a separate
    written instrument signed by Owner (or Owner’s authorized agent) that states:
    (a) the specific Covered Works;
    (b) the exact rights granted (and those reserved);
    (c) territory, term, exclusivity, and compensation if any;
    (d) confidentiality, attribution, and termination terms;
    (e) ownership of improvements and feedback.

5.3 Inbound Contributions. If Owner accepts a contribution from a third party,
    that contribution must be accompanied by an assignment or license sufficient
    for Owner to incorporate it under this instrument. Unsolicited contributions
    do not create joint ownership unless Owner agrees in writing.

5.4 Feedback. Suggestions, ideas, or feedback provided to Owner may be used by
    Owner without obligation or compensation, and Owner may own resulting
    implementations, unless a prior written agreement states otherwise.

================================================================================
6. CONFIDENTIALITY AND PRIVATE MATERIALS
================================================================================
6.1 Private Repositories and Vaults. Materials marked private, held in private
    repositories, or stored in designated vaults are confidential. Unauthorized
    access, disclosure, or use is prohibited.

6.2 Secrets. Credentials, API keys, payment data, personal data, and unpublished
    commercial records must not appear in public repositories and remain under
    separate security and privacy controls.

================================================================================
7. TRADEMARKS AND BRANDING
================================================================================
7.1 Marks. "Cyber Lazer Mermicorn," "Mermicorn Grove," related logos, and trade
    dress originated by Owner are proprietary identifiers. No trademark license
    is granted by this instrument.

7.2 No Confusion. Third parties may not use Owner’s marks in a way likely to
    cause confusion as to source, sponsorship, or affiliation.

================================================================================
8. CREATIVE AND COMMERCIAL WORKS
================================================================================
8.1 Designs and Collections. Original fashion, ravewear, and product design
    concepts, mockups, and packages remain Owner’s exclusive property until and
    unless transferred by written agreement.

8.2 Production Partners. Manufacturers, sewers, and vendors receive only the
    limited rights needed to perform under their separate agreements. Production
    capacity is partnered; Owner does not claim in-house manufacturing unless
    stated.

8.3 AI-Assisted Assets. Outputs generated with AI tools under Owner’s direction
    remain subject to Owner’s rights to the fullest extent permitted by law.
    Tool provider terms may impose additional conditions; those do not expand
    third-party rights in Owner’s directed works beyond those terms.

