================================================================================
TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, OWNER SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY
INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, EXEMPLARY, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES,
OR ANY LOSS OF PROFITS, DATA, OR GOODWILL, ARISING OUT OF OR RELATED TO THE
COVERED WORKS OR THIS INSTRUMENT, WHETHER IN CONTRACT, TORT, OR OTHERWISE,
EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES. OWNER’S TOTAL LIABILITY
FOR ANY CLAIM ARISING OUT OF THE COVERED WORKS SHALL NOT EXCEED ONE HUNDRED
U.S. DOLLARS (US $100), EXCEPT WHERE LIABILITY CANNOT BE LIMITED BY LAW.

================================================================================
11. TERMINATION
================================================================================
11.1 Any limited permission under Section 4 or under a separate written license
     terminates automatically upon material breach of this instrument or of that
     license, or upon written notice from Owner.

11.2 Upon termination, the affected party must cease use of the Covered Works
     and destroy or return copies in their possession, except for copies required
     to be retained by law.

11.3 Sections 1–3, 6–10, 12–14 survive termination.

================================================================================
12. GOVERNING LAW AND VENUE
================================================================================
12.1 Governing Law. This instrument is governed by the laws of the State of
     Hawaiʻi and applicable United States federal law (including the Copyright
     Act), without regard to conflict-of-law principles that would require
     application of another jurisdiction’s laws.

12.2 Venue. Subject to Section 12.3, exclusive venue for disputes arising under
     this instrument lies in the state or federal courts located in the First
     Circuit, City and County of Honolulu, State of Hawaiʻi.

12.3 Escalation. Before filing suit, the parties shall attempt good-faith
     informal resolution, then mediation in Honolulu, Hawaiʻi, unless Owner
     elects to proceed directly for urgent injunctive relief to protect IP.

12.4 Injunctive Relief. Owner may seek temporary, preliminary, or permanent
     injunctive relief in any court of competent jurisdiction to prevent
     ongoing or threatened infringement or misappropriation, without waiving
     the venue provisions for other claims.

================================================================================
13. GENERAL
================================================================================
13.1 Severability. If any provision is held unenforceable, the remainder continues
     in effect, and the unenforceable provision shall be modified to the minimum
     extent necessary to make it enforceable.

13.2 No Waiver. Failure to enforce any provision is not a waiver of future
     enforcement.

13.3 Entire Instrument. This instrument, together with any separate written
     license signed by Owner, constitutes the entire statement of rights for the
     Covered Works as against the public. Platform terms (e.g., GitHub) apply to
     platform use but do not expand substantive IP licenses beyond this instrument.

13.4 Amendments. Owner may update this instrument by publishing a new version
     in the canonical repository (mermicorn-grove). Continued public availability
     after notice constitutes the updated terms for future viewing; prior
     separate written licenses remain governed by their own terms.

13.5 Notices. Notices to Owner regarding this instrument should be sent through
     channels designated on the Cyber Lazer Mermicorn profile or mermicorn-grove
     repository, and by any formal method Owner publishes.

13.6 Export and Sanctions. Users are responsible for compliance with applicable
     export control and sanctions laws.

13.7 Relationship to Individual Repositories. Individual repositories may include
     a short NOTICE pointing to this instrument as the controlling rights text.
     In case of conflict, this instrument controls unless a later signed agreement
     expressly supersedes it for specific works.

